<p>
  Ember 2.0 shipped in August 2015. The
  {{link-to-blank 'Road to Ember 2.0 RFC'
                  'https://github.com/emberjs/rfcs/blob/master/text/0015-the-road-to-ember-2-0.md#onward'}}
  called it the transformation from simply an MVC framework to a complete front-end stack.
  Controllers gave way to a Model-Route-Component-Service mental model, Glimmer brought a virtual DOM,
  and Ember CLI became first-class. The 2.0 release itself mostly removed APIs already deprecated on the 1.x train.
</p>
